  "rationale": "The city's official provider player page (provider-player) titles recording 56029 'Citizen Advisory Committee - Addison, TX' for Jun 01, 2007, with a video index of CAC subject areas (Recreation and Community Facilities, Education, Business Development, Environmental Design, Museums, Performing and Visual Arts, Public Relations, Transportation, Culinary, Human Services). The City Secretary packet (citizen-council-june2007) corroborates the CAC's municipal role: the Addison City Council handled 'the Process for Receiving the Citizen Advisory Committee Recommendations.' Ownership by the City of Addison is therefore established, and the convened body is the Citizen Advisory Committee. It is not the City Council: the packet's official Council actions cover other dates and only discuss receiving the CAC's output, so the Council is not a proven participant in a joint session. It is also not proven to be the Comprehensive Plan Advisory Committee or any other configured body, and per the identity rule the convened body name governs over topic overlap. No existing feed slug corresponds to the Citizen Advisory Committee; inventing one is prohibited, and the public-input family feed (town halls, community meetings, open houses, historical citizen input) does not cover a standing advisory committee's own proceedings. Under the sparse rule, a real municipal body without an existing feed is unconfigured_body rather than non-city or unresolved."
